.TH IRRD-NG 1 "" "irrd-ng" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
irrd-ng \- Internet Routing Registry daemon, drop-in replacement for IRRd 4.5
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B irrd-ng
.I tool
.RI [ arguments ...]
.br
.B irrd
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-foreground ]
.br
.B irrd-ng migrate-check
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-quiet " | " \-\-json ]
.br
.B irrd-ng import \-\-from-postgres
.I dsn
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B irrd-ng
is a drop-in replacement for IRRd 4.5, the Internet Routing Registry
daemon. It reads the same
.IR irrd.yaml ,
answers whois and HTTP queries as IRRd 4.5.4 does, and keeps its data in
an embedded store instead of PostgreSQL and Redis.
.PP
It is one binary installed under several names. Started under one of the
names IRRd v4 installs, it behaves as that tool, with the same options,
output and exit codes:
.BR irrd ,
.BR irrdctl ,
.BR irrd_submit_email ,
.BR irrd_load_database ,
.BR irrd_update_database ,
.BR irrd_mirror_force_reload ,
.BR irrd_set_last_modified_auth ,
.BR irrd_expire_journal ,
.BR irrd_load_pgp_keys ,
.BR irr_rpsl_submit ,
.B irrd_database_upgrade
and
.BR irrd_database_downgrade .
Run as
.BR irrd-ng ,
the first argument names the tool instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B import \-\-from-postgres \fIdsn\fP
Import an IRRd 4.5 PostgreSQL database into the store, read-only on the
source and keeping every NRTM serial. The
.I dsn
may be the
.B database_url
from
.IR irrd.yaml .
Run it as the user irrd-ng runs as.
.TP
.B migrate-check
Check whether irrd-ng can take over from IRRd v4 on this host: whether v4
is still running, whether the store holds an imported database, the size
of the v4 database and whether there is enough free disk space for the
import. It prints the steps that remain. Exit codes: 0 ready to start, 10
IRRd v4 (or another program on its ports) is running, 11 the store is not
imported, 12 not enough disk space for the import, 13 configuration
problem, 2 usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IRRD_NG_STORE_PATH
The store directory, by default
.IR /var/lib/irrd-ng .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/irrd.yaml
The configuration, the same file IRRd v4 reads.
.TP
.I /var/lib/irrd-ng
The store.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/irrd-ng.service
The systemd unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR /usr/share/doc/irrd-ng/README.md ,
.I /usr/share/doc/irrd-ng/docs/migration.md
